# Vite build output (generated by make ui-server-build).
#
# None of it is tracked. The bundle filenames are content-hashed, so a tracked
# index.html goes stale the moment anyone rebuilds, and it would point the embed
# at asset names that are not on disk. The assets themselves cannot be tracked
# either: the JS bundle is over the 500KB check-added-large-files limit, and
# committing a rebuilt bundle on every UI change is what this repo already
# avoids elsewhere.
#
# .gitkeep is the exception, and it is load-bearing: embed.go declares
# `//go:embed all:dist`, which fails to compile if the directory has no files at
# all. Keeping the sentinel tracked means `go build ./...` works in a fresh
# clone; the build steps that repopulate dist/ restore it after wiping it.
dist/*
!dist/.gitkeep

# Static export left behind by the pre-Vite dashboard.
out/
